From 1e8af7272f94ece4f0ba99265ccd15a4c9836a71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felucca dev <dev@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:33:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Eight sequences per track (FELUCCA_PATBANK)

Each track plays one of eight sequences, each with its own steps, LEN and
automation (64 records while it is not the one playing).

- SEQ > SEQUENCE (third SEQ page): KNOB 1..4 pick the sequence of tracks 1..4
- SEQ held + C5..G5: the selected track's sequence; DRUM lane RANDOM moves
  from C5 to F4
- project SAVE/LOAD and the autosave keep the sequences (patbank.c,
  patbank_store.c): five stores of six objects in the flash the three user
  sample slots had, which builds with FELUCCA_PATBANK=1 (default) do not have
  (FELUCCA_USERSMP, the editor's sample commands answer rc 1)
- the project record is unchanged (it holds the sequence that plays)
- tests/patbank_test.c; ui tests updated for the third SEQ page and F4
